                "headline": "Air Quality Alert issued July 28 at 11:17AM PDT by NWS Spokane WA",
                "description": "An Air Quality Alert has been issued by the following agencies:\n\nWashington Department of Ecology\nColville Confederated Tribes\nEnvironmental Protection Agency\n\nAn Air Quality Alert has been issued for Asotin, Chelan, Douglas,\nFerry, Okanogan, and Stevens Counties through Wednesday 11 am due\nto current and expected wildfire smoke from regional fires. Areas\nimmediately downwind of active and emerging fires in Washington\nand Oregon may reach Unhealthy levels of particulate matter\n(PM2.5). When air quality is unhealthy, everyone should reduce\nexposure. Limit time outside, avoid strenuous outdoor activity,\nand follow tips for cleaner indoor air.",
